       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Esmé Cowles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>FWIW, it looks like the initial export has one copy of those rdf:type statements, and the second export has two copies.  So I wouldn't characterize these differences as \"semantic\" — repeating the rdf type statements should not matter.</p>\n\n<p>That said, I think this indicates that we are explicitly creating a statement that is actually a server-generated statement.  We shouldn't be doing that because it might lead to other problems.</p>",
     "created": "15/May/17 5:08 PM",
